\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lo, God is here! Let us adore,
\par And own how dreadful is this place!
\par Let all within us feel His power,
\par And silent bow before His face;
\par Who know His power, His grace
\par who prove,
\par Serve Him with awe, with reverence
\par love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lo, God is here! Him day and night
\par The united choirs of angels sing;
\par To Him, enthroned above all height,
\par Heaven's host their noblest praises bring:
\par Disdain not, Lord, our meaner song
\par Who praise Thee with a stammeering
\par tongue.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Being of brings! May our praise
\par Thy courts with grateful fragrance fill;
\par Still may we stand before Thy face,
\par Still hear and do Thy sovereign will;
\par To Thee may all our thoughts arise,
\par Ceaseless, accepted sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. As flowers their opening leaves display,
\par And glad drink in the solar fire,
\par So may we catch Thy every ray;
\par So may Thy influence us inspire;
\par Thou Beam of the eternal Beam,
\par Thou purging Fire, Thou quickening
\par flame.
\par                      Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

